# BasicForge Grammar (EBNF)

**Version:** 0.1  
**Format:** ISO/IEC 14977 Extended Backus-Naur Form  
**Status:** Milestone 3 target (describes intended grammar; subset implemented)

## Lexical tokens

```ebnf
letter = "A" | "B" | ... | "Z" | "a" | "b" | ... | "z" .
digit  = "0" | "1" | ... | "9" .
idstart = letter | "_" .
idpart = idstart | digit .

identifier = idstart { idpart } .

integer = digit { digit } .
double = digit { digit } "." digit { digit } .
string = '"' { char } '"' .
```

Comments begin with `'` and end at newline. Whitespace (space, tab, CR, LF)
separates tokens but is otherwise insignificant.

Keywords are case-insensitive. `End X` is always two tokens.

## Grammar

```ebnf
program = { module } .

module = "Module" identifier { procedure | class } "End" "Module" .

procedure = sub | function .

sub = "Sub" identifier "(" [ parameterList ] ")" [ "As" type ] block "End" "Sub" .

function = "Function" identifier "(" [ parameterList ] ")" "As" type block "End" "Function" .

parameterList = parameter { "," parameter } .
parameter = identifier "As" type .

block = { statement } .

statement = dimStmt
        | printStmt
        | returnStmt
        | ifStmt
        | forStmt
        | whileStmt
        | selectStmt
        | expressionStmt
        | assignmentStmt   {planned}
        | callStmt .

dimStmt = "Dim" identifier [ "As" type ] [ "=" expression ] .

printStmt = "Print" "(" expression { "," expression } ")" .

returnStmt = "Return" [ expression ] .

ifStmt = "If" expression "Then" block [ "Else" block ] "End" "If" .

forStmt = "For" identifier "As" type "=" expression "To" expression [ "Step" expression ] block "Next" .

whileStmt = "While" expression block "End" "While" .

selectStmt = "Select" "Case" expression { caseClause } "End" "Select" .

caseClause = "Case" expression { "," expression } block
         | "Case" "Else" block .

expressionStmt = expression .

callStmt = identifier "(" [ argumentList ] ")" .

argumentList = expression { "," expression } .

assignmentStmt = identifier "=" expression . {planned}

type = "Integer" | "Long" | "Single" | "Double" | "Boolean" | "String" .

expression = equalityExpr .

equalityExpr = comparisonExpr { ("=" | "<>") comparisonExpr } .

comparisonExpr = term { ("<" | ">" | "<=" | ">=") term } .

term = factor { ("+" | "-" | "&") factor } .

factor = unary { ("*" | "/" | "\" | "Mod" | "^") unary } .

unary = ["-" | "Not"] unary | primary .

primary = integerLiteral
        | doubleLiteral
        | stringLiteral
        | "True" | "False"
        | identifier
        | "(" expression ")"
        | callExpr .

callExpr = identifier "(" [ argumentList ] ")" .

class = "Class" identifier "End" "Class" . {planned}
```

## Notes

- `End If`, `End Sub`, `End Function`, `End While`, `End Select`, `End Module`,
  `End Class` are always two tokens.
- `Case Else` is two tokens.
- `Dim x = initializer` (type inference) requires the initializer; `As type` is
  optional only when an initializer is present.
- `Step` in `For` defaults to 1 when omitted.
- Assignment and user-defined types (class, enum, structure) are planned and
  not yet in the implemented grammar.
